# cooling_envelope, redback 1.20.0's bundled prior, regenerated verbatim.
#
# Source: redback.priors.get_priors('cooling_envelope'), serialised with
# PriorDict.to_file(). Distributions, bounds and latex labels are identical to
# redback/priors/cooling_envelope.prior; only the written form differs (explicit keyword
# arguments instead of positional). Checked by
# tests/test_redback_pipeline.py::test_prior_files_match_redback.
#
# Versioned here so a bound can be changed deliberately, and so a redback upgrade
# that moves one shows up as a test failure instead of silently changing a fit.
#
# Physical constraints are NOT in this file: they are Constraint priors attached
# by get_priors(model, constraint=True) and added by fit_redback.build_priors.
#
# Preserved from redback's own cooling_envelope.prior:
#   eta > eta_min(mbh_6, stellar_mass) and beta < beta_max(mbh_6, stellar_mass)
#   must hold for physical solutions. These bounds depend on sampled parameter
#   combinations, so pass constraint=True to get_priors() or fit_model() to have
#   bilby reject invalid samples automatically.
# fit_redback.build_priors does exactly that, and raises if the Constraint priors
# turn out to be absent, attaching only a conversion function computes the
# constraint and then ignores it.

redshift = Uniform(minimum=1e-06, maximum=3, name='redshift', latex_label='$z$', unit=None, boundary=None)
mbh_6 = LogUniform(minimum=0.1, maximum=10, name='mbh_6', latex_label='$M_{\\mathrm{BH}}~[10^{6}~M_{\\odot}]$', unit=None, boundary=None)
stellar_mass = LogUniform(minimum=0.5, maximum=10, name='stellar_mass', latex_label='$M_{\\mathrm{star}}[M_{\\odot}]$', unit=None, boundary=None)
eta = LogUniform(minimum=0.0001, maximum=0.1, name='eta', latex_label='$\\eta$', unit=None, boundary=None)
alpha = LogUniform(minimum=0.1, maximum=1, name='alpha', latex_label='$\\alpha$', unit=None, boundary=None)
beta = Uniform(minimum=1, maximum=5, name='beta', latex_label='$\\beta$', unit=None, boundary=None)
